<Base title="How I assess agent research" description="Proof standards, provenance, correction history, and what retained agent traces can establish.">
  <p><a href="/research">Research</a></p>
  <h1>How I assess agent research</h1>
  <p>I want a reader to be able to check the result and inspect the work that produced it.
    Those require different evidence.</p>
  <h2>The mathematics</h2>
  <p>A counterexample needs the exact original statement, an explicit witness, and a calculation that establishes the violating sign.
    A family that defeats every coefficient also needs an argument for the whole family.
    A long table of numerical examples cannot prove an infinite limit.</p>
  <p>I distinguish a replay of the original checker, a fresh implementation, an independent reconstruction of the argument, and external review.
    Agreement between sibling agents is useful, but shared inputs and shared mistakes can survive it.</p>
  <p>Correctness and novelty are separate judgments.
    Reproducing a known construction can be valuable verification without being a new discovery.
    An unattributed input corpus does not become an agent discovery because a later run reproduced it.</p>
  <h2>The agent work</h2>
  <p>The viewer reads publication projections of retained execution records.
    Runtime journals identify recorded agents and parent-child relations.
    Native transcripts identify harness sessions, model observations, message records, and provider usage counters.
    A native session is joined to a Runtime agent only when the source establishes that relationship.</p>
  <p>Each displayed event includes a source-file hash and line number.
    Unresolved joins remain separate lanes.
    The download contains the published event metadata; the original private records are preserved separately.</p>
  <p>Unreviewed transcript bodies, credentials, private reasoning, and unrelated personal information are excluded from the public projection.
    This exclusion is recorded explicitly.
    A publication projection is not advertised as a complete raw transcript.</p>
  <h2>Reading the timeline</h2>
  <p>Marks show recorded events, and vertical links show recorded delegation.
    The spaces between marks do not measure uninterrupted work or idle time.
    Category colors use documented tool and command rules, so “verification” indicates an operation classified as checking, not an independently verified theorem.</p>
  <p>Token trajectories sum retained provider usage counters.
    Repeated prompts and cached context count repeatedly.
    Missing sessions are omitted, and unknown billing is never shown as zero cost.</p>
  <p>I do not classify spending as waste merely because it produced no positive finding.
    A useful failed search can eliminate an approach.
    Judging waste requires the attempted objective, what the agent knew then, and the evidence it left behind.</p>
  <h2>Corrections stay attached</h2>
  <p>The invalid BCWW smoke witness remains part of the history.
    Its replacement has its own exact statement and verification.
    Earlier “winner” labels are preserved as execution history; they cannot overrule a later mathematical correction.</p>
  <p>The current pages expose incomplete archives rather than reconstruct a plausible story around them.
    More source bytes can extend a record later, with a new dated assessment and visible changes.</p>
